#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# to_radicals

#% text
# `to_radicals(e)` replaces every `root_sum` in `e` whose polynomial is an irreducible cubic or quartic by the sum over its roots written with radicals.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The roots are the ones `solve` gives by the cubic and quartic formulas, so they may contain complex radicals even when the sum is real.

#% item
# Sums over polynomials of other degrees stay as they are.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A sum of logarithms over the roots of a pure cubic:

#% cell
to_radicals(root_sum(x => x^3 - 2, x => x*log(z - x)))
#% output
#= log(z - 2^(1/3))*2^(1/3) + log(z - (-1)^(2/3)*2^(1/3))*(-1)^(2/3)*2^(1/3) - log(z + (-1)^(1/3)*2^(1/3))*(-1)^(1/3)*2^(1/3)

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The numeric value does not change:

#% cell
n(to_radicals(root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => log(2 - x))))
#% output
#= 2.3978952727983702 + 0.0im

#% cell
n(root_sum(x => x^3 + x + 1, x => log(2 - x)))
#% output
#= 2.3978952727983702

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `root_sum`, `solve`, `root`
